description:
Wire drafting-model grading end to end. This spans TWO files and THREE edits; it is only meaningful when all land, so apply all three. A previous attempt was correctly refused as a stub because it stored the model but never reported it - this version includes the reporting call.

FILE 1 — repos/llm-resolver-vessel/src/index.ts. Replace this line, which occurs exactly once:
  ["llmQuotaState", llmQuotaStateHandler as never],

with:
  ["llmArmOutcome_write", (async (ctx: { body: unknown }) => {
    const b = ctx.body as { model?: string; reached?: boolean; task_type?: string };
    if (!b || typeof b.model !== "string" || typeof b.reached !== "boolean") {
      return { resolved: false, shape: "llmArmOutcomeWriteResult", error: "body must include model as a string and reached as a boolean" };
    }
    await recordArmOutcome(b.model, b.reached, b.task_type);
    return { resolved: true, shape: "llmArmOutcomeWriteResult", body: { graded: b.model, reached: b.reached } };
  }) as never],
  ["llmQuotaState", (llmQuotaStateHandler) as never],

FILE 2 — repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/feature-compose.ts, edit A. Replace this line, which occurs exactly once:
  console.log("[fc-draft-model] selected=" + String((j as { model_selection?: { selected?: unknown } })?.model_selection?.selected ?? "unknown") + " task=feature_compose");

with:
  const __sel = String((j as { model_selection?: { selected?: unknown } })?.model_selection?.selected ?? "unknown");
  if (__sel !== "unknown") {
    (globalThis as Record<string, unknown>).__fcDraftModel = __sel;
    (globalThis as Record<string, unknown>).__fcDraftEndpoint = endpoint;
  }
  console.log("[fc-draft-model] pick=" + __sel + " task=feature_compose");

FILE 2 — edit B. Replace these two consecutive lines, which occur exactly once:
    writeFileSync(
      reportPath,

with:
    void (async () => {
      try {
        const gm = String((globalThis as Record<string, unknown>).__fcDraftModel ?? "");
        const ge = String((globalThis as Record<string, unknown>).__fcDraftEndpoint ?? "");
        if (!gm || !ge) return;
        const gr = verdict === "FAVORABLE";
        await fetch(ge, {
          method: "POST",
          headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json", Authorization: "ApiKey " + METABOB_API_KEY },
          body: JSON.stringify({ type: "llmArmOutcome_write", model: gm, reached: gr, task_type: "feature_compose" }),
        });
        console.log("[fc-draft-model] graded=" + gm + " reached=" + String(gr));
      } catch { /* grading is best effort */ }
    })();
    writeFileSync(
      (reportPath),

How the three connect: edit A records which model drafted and the endpoint that served it; edit B, once the compose verdict is final, reports that model and whether it reached to the new shaped endpoint added by file 1; file 1's handler forwards it to recordArmOutcome, which already maintains the per-task task_alpha and task_beta posteriors. Nothing is stored without being used and nothing is added without a caller.

Why it matters: recordArmOutcome already grades the seven task types that have posteriors. Drafting - feature_compose and patch_with_tools - is excluded from immediate grading and the deferred grader was never wired, so those two carry ZERO learned posterior and model choice for authoring code rides on reputation earned at unrelated tasks. METABOB_API_KEY is already in scope in file 2. The grading call is fire-and-forget inside a try block, so it cannot affect any verdict.

